Add a local MaxMind GeoIP2 provider plugin (no remote rate limiting)

Issue: https://www.drupal.org/project/webform_ip_geo/issues/3556190

The bundled ipapi.co provider performs a remote HTTP lookup for every webform
submission. On even modestly trafficked sites ipapi.co returns HTTP 429
"Too Many Requests", surfacing as an uncaught
GuzzleHttp\Exception\ClientException in the log.

This adds a webform_ip_geo_geoip2 sub-module providing a "geoip2" provider
plugin backed by an on-disk MaxMind GeoIP2 / GeoLite2 City database (*.mmdb).
Lookups run locally via the geoip2/geoip2 PHP library, so there is no API and
no rate limit. It exposes the same tokens as the ipapi.co provider ([city],
[region], [region_code], [country_code], [country_name]; [country_code_iso3]
is empty as GeoLite2 lacks the alpha-3 code), so switching provider on the
settings form is a drop-in change.

The database path is read solely from this module's own configuration
(webform_ip_geo_geoip2.settings:database), configurable at
/admin/config/services/webform_ip_geo/geoip2. No other modules are involved.

